LumenShell is a ChromeOS-inspired desktop shell for Wayland, built on the
Wayfire compositor: a panel with control center, app drawer, notifications,
on-screen display, lock screen, polkit agent and a settings app, written in
Vala with GTK 4 and gtk4-layer-shell.

On FreeBSD it uses the native stack: OSS through mixer(8), backlight(9),
wpa_supplicant(8)/ifconfig(8) for networking, ConsoleKit2 or shutdown(8)
for power, OpenPAM for unlocking and syslogd(8) for logs.
